    board: file CF-116 — the census coverage assertion counts rows, so a mid-run insert yields a duplicate plus a hole and still exits 0
    
    QA re-verification of CF-089 (commit 61db6f7, verdict 7c2c8c8d bound to 61db6f7, passed=true)
    reproduces its accepted fix at 0c765f6: the 502 leg aborts with "census: HTTP 502 at
    offset=500; refusing to count" at rc=1, the short-page leg (arm 25, 865 != 866) fails closed, the
    live census still prints 19 rows at rc=0, and selftest carries arms 22-28 for the class. Those
    criteria are met, so CF-089 stays complete.
    
    The failure CF-089 did not test is the same shape one step further out: its coverage assertion is
    a COUNT. Offset pagination over a list that mutates between two fetches shifts every later
    offset, so a project inserted mid-run makes the census receive exactly `total` rows while one row
    is served twice and another is never served.
    
    Reproduced at 0c765f6 with the stand-in added here (docs/audits/cf116-census-dup-standin.py):
    page offset=0 serves rows 0..499 of 600, page offset=500 serves row 499 again and never row 500.
    
      BASE=http://127.0.0.1:18996 bash docs/audits/cf089-census-recipe.sh
      -> census_rc=0, row_lines=600, distinct_rows=599, p500=MISSING, p499_occurrences=2
    
    The recipe prints "600" and 600 plausible row lines; nothing in the tree enumerates identities
    (rows are appended blindly with jq -c '.projects[]' and the only assertion is received == total).
    Scheduler project rows carry id=null, so .name is the identity key. This is CF-089's own trigger
    class — a scheduler restart or load-shed between two pages — reached by an insert instead of a
    502, and it produces the plausible short-count output CF-089 was filed to prevent.
    
    CF-116 is filed pending with a probe that reproduces the leg from the committed board, and an
    acceptance list that requires identity coverage (duplicate/distinct vs total, named identity), the
    same change in README.md and the executable mirror, a falsifiable selftest arm, and the live
    census still at 19 rows. The new file is a fixture only: no recipe or selftest arm is touched, so
    the gap still reproduces at this commit.
    
    Board write: one appended row plus one task_created event (126). Row count 89 -> 90, events
    125 -> 126, insertion-only (2 lines, 0 deletions), no duplicate ids, boardctl validate RESULT: OK
    (31 warnings, the probe key sits outside the declared canon by precedent).
    
    Gate: docs/board-only diff, so the guard reports the documented DEGRADED PASS (lint skipped: no
    implementation files staged) and this commit takes the disclosed board/docs-only bypass
    (CF-031 precedent). Tree-wide ruff check . and ruff format --check . both exit 0 at this commit;
    bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS.
    
